        "slc_736bfd374959588c6a44feb9c27243ca4659256e434b6ea4b9e433ad2e555f6f"
      ],
      "text": "Langroid is a Python framework for building LLM applications where users set up Agents equipped with optional components (LLM, vector-store, tools/functions) that collaborate by exchanging messages."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_3191dcf4143f79c4fb19ea234222695139f58cf52755d67df8f048376c2b19bc",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "design-choices",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f",
          "git_sha": "038442b6b4ebca040309a8d7314c4c61ea8fbf35",
          "line_end": 45,
          "line_start": 38,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "langroid/langroid",
          "url": "https://github.com/langroid/langroid/blob/53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f/README.md#L38-L45"
        },
        {
          "commit": "53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f",
          "git_sha": "038442b6b4ebca040309a8d7314c4c61ea8fbf35",
          "line_end": 50,
          "line_start": 47,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "langroid/langroid",
          "url": "https://github.com/langroid/langroid/blob/53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f/README.md#L47-L50"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_736bfd374959588c6a44feb9c27243ca4659256e434b6ea4b9e433ad2e555f6f",
        "slc_f6ed399752416a7986efd113e5fd14280156870e3bdd8bf35a43fe5ea57cbf16"
      ],
      "text": "The multi-agent paradigm is inspired by the Actor model, and the framework does not use LangChain or any other LLM framework, aiming to work with practically any LLM."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_82a9b318f87f6bab08b904e3ceddbf455d44f7628120e764f98a211bcb9096a2",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f",
          "git_sha": "038442b6b4ebca040309a8d7314c4c61ea8fbf35",
          "line_end": 493,
          "line_start": 455,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "langroid/langroid",
          "url": "https://github.com/langroid/langroid/blob/53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f/README.md#L455-L493"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_44f4100f9a4e8b8b53d9ddd56b164674fe8ff9b400ce6798b2eb2a7bc518988b"
      ],
      "text": "The Agent class encapsulates LLM conversation state plus an optional vector-store and tools, acts as a message transformer, and by default provides three responder methods corresponding to LLM, Agent, and User."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_f6b6bb1b173887469c6bc272f026fd36266b6eb3c1e241aa55ca6297870462a3",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "orchestration",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f",
          "git_sha": "038442b6b4ebca040309a8d7314c4c61ea8fbf35",
          "line_end": 493,
          "line_start": 455,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "langroid/langroid",
          "url": "https://github.com/langroid/langroid/blob/53c01d4e1a9e7c1dd829c97513aaf57f23b2945f/README.md#L455-L493"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_44f4100f9a4e8b8b53d9ddd56b164674fe8ff9b400ce6798b2eb2a7bc518988b"
      ],
      "text": "A Task wraps an Agent, manages iteration over the agent's responder methods, and orchestrates multi-agent interaction via hierarchical, recursive task delegation; sub-tasks are treated as additional responders used round-robin after the agent's own responders."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_80fdc521582a18fe7e7fdd580f8894a842527d41b76ecb654c9c982dcd58771a",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "interfaces",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
